From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhugengyu <zhugengyu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] sdio: (xmit) Free a frame whose coalesce fails after the
 first one

The aggregation loop counts coalesced frames in `k`.  It removes a frame
from its queue before coalescing it and, afterwards, frees it only when
`k != 1`.  That test distinguishes "first frame of this buffer, still
owned by the buffer" from "later frame, already copied" only while every
coalesce succeeds: once one frame has been coalesced (k == 1), a failure
on the next frame leaves k at 1, so the frame is neither copied into the
buffer nor freed.  Its xmit frame and the skb it carries are then lost
for the life of the adapter, which shows up as the skb pool filling up
while traffic is idle.

Free the frame on the failure path as well, and keep the success path's
ownership rule unchanged (the first coalesced frame belongs to the
transmit buffer, every later one is released after the copy).

Signed-off-by: zhugengyu <zhugengyu@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 hal/rtl8188f/sdio/rtl8189fs_xmit.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/hal/rtl8188f/sdio/rtl8189fs_xmit.c
+++ b/hal/rtl8188f/sdio/rtl8189fs_xmit.c
@@ -437,7 +437,16 @@
 				ret = rtw_xmitframe_coalesce(padapter, pxmitframe->pkt, pxmitframe);
 				if (ret == _FAIL) {
 					RTW_ERR("%s: coalesce FAIL!", __FUNCTION__);
-					/* Todo: error handler */
+					/*
+					 * The frame left its queue above and no transmit
+					 * buffer owns it.  The "k != 1" test below only
+					 * releases a frame that was not coalesced while k
+					 * was still 0 (the first frame of a buffer); once
+					 * one frame has been coalesced (k == 1) a second
+					 * frame's failure left the xmit frame and its skb
+					 * allocated for the life of the adapter.
+					 */
+					rtw_free_xmitframe(pxmitpriv, pxmitframe);
 				} else {
 					k++;
 					if (k != 1)
@@ -453,7 +462,7 @@
 					pxmitbuf->len = _RND(pxmitbuf->len, 8) + txlen;
 				}
 
-				if (k != 1)
+				if (ret != _FAIL && k != 1)
 					rtw_free_xmitframe(pxmitpriv, pxmitframe);
 				pxmitframe = NULL;
 			}
